# Actions for the selected component in 13.5.21

The original F.9 setup gives a faithful binary action of H/O₂(H) on U_H/V₁
with its generating V₃/V₁ seed and its literal ambient-quotient marking.
Component selection retains K ≤ H, quasisimplicity of K*, the K/O₂(K)
equivalence and the nontrivial V*-commutator. Under explicit simple-section
evenness, the index-two seed gives normalization and K* = [K*,V*].
The 13.5.19 inputs give nontrivial Y*-action, and normalization by L₁*
gives K* = [K*,L₁*] and the faithful action of X/C_X(K*).

These are preparations for Lemma 13.5.21, not its complete six clauses.
The source configuration must still discharge the evenness and L₁*
normalization inputs and prove (i)–(iv). Complete B.4 catalogue elimination,
natural chief-section recognition, L₁ ≤ K, the triple-cover exclusion,
relative normality in H and the marked module/parabolic conclusions remain
with the recognition assembly. The independent 13.5.20 premise is supplied
by the Fitting branch in the enclosing component-reduction assembly.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
Lemma 13.5.21, printed pp.923–924 (PDF pp.940–941).
-/
